@bnellnm this follows up on the `deepep_ll.py` issue you flagged in #64086. The same guard preserves `-1` through the helper shared by dispatch and combine.

The tests reuse the existing NIXL regression with backend-specific adaptations: **6 CPU cases passed**. H200 core checks for the same DeepEP production code passed **3 CUDA adapter cases and 6 adapter CUDA Graph replay configurations**. [Results and reproducer](https://github.com/algebra-MCX/vllm/blob/c2170732ab2585970cb1cb38d70ef8da1a5fe13d/benchmarks/moe/deepep_ll_sentinel_h200_20261028/README.md).

The H200 checks use real CUDA tensors and a recording external transport; native multi-rank communication and model validation remain unestablished. Could you take a look when you have a chance?

